{
  "comment": [
    "A Guardian Rises (act_cosmo_m0_highway): the start of the first mission, as a stand-in activity-host script.",
    "Use with bap_server.py --ah-mission missions/a_guardian_rises.json (see notes/mission-director.md).",
    "Order from the reference recording: revival cinematic (third person, then first person), 'Enter the Wall',",
    "trigger at the Wall, 'Find a Weapon' in The Breach, the Ghost's light, the power beat (pf_104a_pwr), 'Grab the Rifle'.",
    "Field meanings are from the EBOOT handlers; the values marked in the note as guesses are what the runs test.",
    "Triggers (kind 0x1d): +0 true arms the trigger, with the arming time at +4 = \"$now\" and --ah-sim-clock enabled.",
    "01.24 trigger reports are type-18 incidents; repeated reports and the Breach disconnect still need diagnosis.",
    "Objectives: 1 = active; 3 = complete (the handler special-cases 3, and the state-3 case of 0x355abc calls into the",
    "character/progress code); 2 looks like 'active with progress counters'. Squads (kind 1): a new +0x44 generation re-runs",
    "the squad; squad_existing_members means +0x5c on 01.00 or +0x74 on 01.24 (0 destroy, 1 release, -1 nothing).",
    "01.24 JOIN99/101: sq_nux_ghost desired counts at +0x2c = {0:1,4:[1]} create one physical member after bubble readiness and a manual protocol reset.",
    "The Breach state changes are scheduled 20 s after current slice set 24; Fallen desired counts remain unverified.",
    "Objective states (01.24, JOIN60): 1 = incoming (the 'NEW MISSION' banner with the activity name, about 4 s), 5 = active:",
    "the title (and on change its description) shows at the left of the HUD. Each objective is set to 1 and 6 s later to 5.",
    "3 is still used for completion (special-cased by the handler); its on-screen effect is not confirmed yet.",
    "Handover (JOIN70): the completed objective goes to 3 (with its completion sequence), 4 s later to 0 while the next",
    "objective starts (1, incoming sequence step 1, trigger armed), and 6 s after that the next objective goes to 5.",
    "01.24 JOIN77/81: player-trigger reports are type-18 incidents. Objective lane phases cancel delayed updates from earlier handovers.",
    "Breach object names now resolve each signed relative name pointer; the old printable-string scan shifted names by six records.",
    "pf_104a_pwr is the separate power beat; the ho_ghostlight alias enables a bounded manual selector test, with no automatic torch action yet.",
    "01.24 JOIN104: the manual o_device_invis_light alias creates, removes and recreates its placed unit using generation and +4 Boolean; illumination and mission timing remain unverified.",
    "01.24 JOIN109: the authored Ghost member state creates one unit with member/performance bindings while desired counts remain zero; it replaces the count-only Ghost path.",
    "nux_ghost is a manual performance alias, kind 0x28 (40 decimal)/index 125; no automatic cue or torch action is enabled.",
    "01.24 JOIN182: raw kind-13 positions require 96 wire bits even when schema width is zero.",
    "Objective markers use entry 0 at +0x40, type 1, authored nav target at entry+0x20 and null root fallback slice bucket (112>>3=14, 24>>3=3).",
    "JOIN182 verifies the normal-view Enter the Wall diamond and disabled marker after completion; the next three target entries are configured but still need native visibility acceptance.",
    "JOIN186: native incident 734 ends/stops a cinematic; match its measured kind-6 object field, never a started incident or arbitrary ID bits.",
    "Revival handovers now follow those incidents instead of fixed 70/45-second stops. JOIN186 traces all nine third-person scenes, automatic first-person handover and 113-to-112 arrival.",
    "JOIN186 uses a private 90-second initial delay; this script retains the original 20-second start. Its urgent overlay prevents cinematic visual acceptance.",
    "JOIN188: after the natural crossing, a fresh inactive bubble-3 reset (sent manually 85 s after current 24) is followed by Breach sensor traffic and a Ghost radar blip; the reset is now a mission step 10 s after the member/squad states. Its automatic timing still needs a native run.",
    "JOIN190: host-stepped dialogue sequences play (Ghost speaker indicator and voice audio). seq_d_o2_30 is limited to players inside tv_flashlight (the corridor after the doorway, x 346-384), so it starts 2 s after current 24. Its resource is a plain dialogue line; it does not turn the torch on.",
    "JOIN204: line texts come from each sequence's dialogue resource: o2_10 find you a weapon, o2_20 Quiet. They're right above us (now played 2 s after current 24, as in the reference), o2_40 Hang tight, o2_50/o2_60 hardened military systems, o2_70 They're coming for us, o2_80 found a rifle, o2_90 hope you know how to use that thing; o2_30's text is unresolved.",
    "JOIN190: pt_fallen_above (volume x 327-342 inside the Wall) reports once armed and stops when disarmed; the audible/visible effect of seq_fallen_above is not yet verified.",
    "Normal/Nav Mode objective text, complete revival shots/Ghost and stable Breach progression remain incomplete.",
    "JOIN205-207: the light-up start trigger (armed 35 s after current 24, after the bubble-3 reset) plays the reference order: o2_40 Hang tight, +10 s o2_50 hardened military systems, +22 s Breach control/door/gating light props created, +25 s o2_70 They're coming for us, +30 s o2_80 found a rifle. Visible lamp lighting remains unverified.",
    "JOIN208 static correction: o_chest_primary_weapon is placed at (534.865,-736.800,16.507), far from the rifle waypoint. The activity's o_weapon is at (410.644,-794.385,17.723), matching that waypoint. The rifle cue now creates o_weapon instead of the unrelated chest; native pickup and durable inventory grant remain unverified."
  ],
